[5] Proof readout
  S136 turns the C=27 branch into a marked transfer problem.
  Bounded frontier evidence through the S130 single-replacement atlas says:
    M<=3/41 gives exactly AP, GW, and the 12->36 K33 near-miss;
    M<=2/27 adds exactly the two unit-hole petals 10->20 and 13->26.
  This suggests a sharper lemma target:
    after standard reductions, any low-gap non-AP/GW atom must either
    have a unit-visible C=27 hole, hence belongs to the second-gap/petal
    branch, or move a gcd-3 nonunit hole into the gcd-9 shell, hence
    carries the first K33/Farey-child state-lift packet.
  The warning is equally important: shell transfer alone is not the proof.
  The exact Farey branch remains attached to prevent safely loose rows from
  masquerading as frontier rows.
